| **US-22** | As a **System**, I want monetary values to be stored as decimal numbers to avoid rounding errors. | **US-22-AC01** (condition) – Price, unit price, total amount, invoice amount, and payment amount are stored using a decimal type with at least two fractional digits. |
| **US-23** | As a **System**, I want the allowed status values and payment methods to be restricted to the enumerated sets defined in the domain. | **US-23-AC01** (condition) – Order status ∈ {submitted, pending, filled, shipped, closed}. <br> **US-23-AC02** (condition) – Invoice status ∈ {issued, paid}. <br> **US-23-AC03** (condition) – Payment status ∈ {pending, completed, failed}. <br> **US-23-AC04** (condition) – Payment method ∈ {bank, card, cash}. |
| **US-24** | As a **System**, I want status transitions to be limited to the allowed sequences so that the lifecycle is predictable. | **US-24-AC01** (condition) – Order: submitted → pending → filled → shipped → closed (or submitted → pending → closed). <br> **US-24-AC02** (condition) – Invoice: issued → paid. <br> **US-24-AC03** (condition) – Payment: pending → completed OR pending → failed. |

*The above 24 user stories together realise all 50 functional domain requirements. Acceptance criteria reference the specific rules (e.g., multiplicities, status changes) that were originally expressed as REQ‑F‑xx.*

## 3.2 Quality attributes
### 3.2.1 Performance
| ID | Statement |
|----|-----------|
| **NFR-01** | **REQ‑N‑01** When a user submits an order containing up to 50 order items under normal operating conditions, the system shall register the order and respond within 2 seconds for at least 95 % of submissions. |
| **NFR-02** | **REQ‑N‑02** Under normal operating conditions, the system shall support at least 200 concurrent users and at least 20 order submissions per second while meeting the response time of NFR‑01. |

### 3.2.2 Security
| ID | Statement |
|----|-----------|
| **NFR-03** | **REQ‑N‑05** The system shall authenticate every user before granting access to any customer, order, invoice or payment data, and shall reject 100 % of unauthenticated requests. |
| **NFR-04** | **REQ‑N‑06** The system shall allow only users holding the accountant role to confirm or reject a payment, and shall reject the same request from any other user. |
| **NFR-05** | **REQ‑N‑07** The system shall protect customer personal data and bank account numbers by encrypting them in transit with TLS 1.2 or higher and at rest. |
| **NFR-06** | **REQ‑N‑08** The system shall record the user and the time of every status change of an order, an invoice and a payment, and shall retain these records for at least 12 months. |

### 3.2.3 Availability
| ID | Statement |
|----|-----------|
| **NFR-07** | **REQ‑N‑03** The system shall be available for at least 99.5 % of each calendar month, excluding scheduled maintenance announced at least 24 hours in advance. |
| **NFR-08** | **REQ‑N‑04** When a server failure occurs, the system shall resume accepting requests within 15 minutes without losing any order, invoice or payment recorded before the failure. |

# 4. Verification
Verification of each functional requirement shall be performed by automated unit and integration tests that exercise the given‑when‑then scenarios and validate the condition constraints. Non‑functional requirements shall be verified by performance load testing, security penetration testing, and availability monitoring as described in the test plan.

